From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] PCI: host-common: ROG5: keep the link for wakeup-enabled devices

pci_host_common_d3cold_possible() lets dw_pcie_suspend_noirq() stop the link
and deinit the host when a wakeup-enabled device reports PME from D3cold.
The upstream TODO notes that this should also require Vaux, which this board
does not provide: with Wake-on-WLAN armed (ath11k sets the WCN6855 wakeup
enabled) the deinit asserted PERST#, the chip came back reset on resume
("mhi mhi0: Resuming from non M3 state (RESET)", qrtr_mhi resume -22), and
it could not have woken the system while suspended.

Treat a wakeup-enabled device as blocking D3cold. Without Wake-on-WLAN the
link still powers down in suspend (0073).

--- a/drivers/pci/controller/pci-host-common.c	2026-09-27 16:02:53.128520186 +0200
+++ b/drivers/pci/controller/pci-host-common.c	2026-09-27 16:02:53.142229580 +0200
@@ -294,12 +294,15 @@
 	if (pdev->current_state != PCI_D3hot)
 		goto exit;
 
-	if (device_may_wakeup(&pdev->dev)) {
-		if (!pci_pme_capable(pdev, PCI_D3cold))
-			goto exit;
-		else
-			*flags |= PCI_HOST_PME_D3COLD_CAPABLE;
-	}
+	/*
+	 * ROG5: a wakeup-enabled endpoint keeps its link. The WCN6855 reports
+	 * PME from D3cold, but the board has no Vaux for it, and the host
+	 * deinit asserts PERST#: with WoWLAN armed the chip came back reset
+	 * ("Resuming from non M3 state (RESET)") and could not have woken the
+	 * system. Without wakeup the link still powers down in suspend.
+	 */
+	if (device_may_wakeup(&pdev->dev))
+		goto exit;
 
 	return 0;
 
